# Phase 1b: operator-supplied SHARED free-tier key for google, used by every
# user of this PAWN deployment when they hold no BYOK key of their own for
# google (or ahead of it, per the pool-first precedence -- see
# app/config.py's read_pool_key() and resolver.py's _resolve_key()).
#
# This is YOUR OWN google free-tier signup, not a key you were given by
# someone else -- see workspace/plan/router_failover's Phase 1b design notes
# on why self-hosting keeps this within each provider's ToS.
#
# To enable: copy this file to secrets/pool_google_api_key (no .example),
# put your real key inside, then add pool_google_api_key to BOTH the
# top-level secrets: block and the backend service's secrets: list in
# docker-compose.yml, then restart. Leaving it unconfigured is completely
# safe -- every endpoint just falls back to BYOK exactly as before.
REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_GOOGLE_API_KEY
